{"id":"B5","lessons":[{"id":"B5-L1","recap":[{"back_html":"nullable=False. Set nullable=True where nulls are expected.","front_html":"pandera Column defaults"},{"back_html":"strict rejects unknown columns. coerce converts dtypes before checks.","front_html":"strict=True and coerce=True"},{"back_html":"Runs every check and raises SchemaErrors with failure_cases.","front_html":"validate(df, lazy=True)"},{"back_html":"Separate classes. SchemaErrors is not a subclass. Catch both, or better, let them raise.","front_html":"SchemaError vs SchemaErrors"}],"snippets":[["<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">pandera.pandas</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">as</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">pa</span>","","<span class=\"n\">RESPONSES</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">pa</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">DataFrameSchema</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>","    <span class=\"p\">{</span>","        <span class=\"s2\">\"respondent_id\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">pa</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Column</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">unique</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>","        <span class=\"s2\">\"age\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">pa</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Column</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">int</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">pa</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Check</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">in_range</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">16</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mi\">99</span><span class=\"p\">)),</span>","        <span class=\"s2\">\"weight\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">pa</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Column</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nb\">float</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">pa</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Check</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">gt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)),</span>","    <span class=\"p\">},</span>","    <span class=\"n\">strict</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>","    <span class=\"n\">coerce</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>","<span class=\"p\">)</span>","<span class=\"n\">clean</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">RESPONSES</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">validate</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">lazy</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>"]],"takeaway_html":"A schema at the point of entry turns a silent bad input into one loud, detailed failure.","title":"DataFrame schemas with pandera"},{"id":"B5-L2","recap":[{"back_html":"Ignored silently. Use ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\") for config.","front_html":"pydantic extra keys, default behaviour"},{"back_html":"Converts \"30\" and 30.0 to 30, True to 1. Use strict=True to refuse conversions.","front_html":"pydantic lax mode"},{"back_html":"Does not validate. Rebuild with model_validate({**m.model_dump(), ...}).","front_html":"model_copy(update=...)"},{"back_html":"pydantic for records and settings from outside. pandera for whole DataFrames.","front_html":"pydantic or pandera"}],"snippets":[["<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">pydantic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">BaseModel</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">ConfigDict</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">Field</span>","","","<span class=\"k\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">WeightingConfig</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">BaseModel</span><span class=\"p\">):</span>","    <span class=\"n\">model_config</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">ConfigDict</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">extra</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"forbid\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">frozen</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>","","    <span class=\"n\">weight_col</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>","    <span class=\"n\">min_base</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">int</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">50</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">gt</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>","    <span class=\"n\">cap</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">float</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">5.0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">gt</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">1.0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>","","","<span class=\"n\">cfg</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">WeightingConfig</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">model_validate</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">yaml</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">safe_load</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>"]],"takeaway_html":"Validate external settings and records once, at the boundary, with every rule in the model.","title":"pydantic models for config and input records"},{"id":"B5-L3","recap":[{"back_html":"At boundaries: after reading input, before writing output.","front_html":"Where to validate"},{"back_html":"CRITICAL stops the run (raise). WARN records and continues.","front_html":"CRITICAL vs WARN"},{"back_html":"Run every check, log all results, then raise if any CRITICAL failed.","front_html":"Order of QA operations"},{"back_html":"Guard every division. Test for None with is None, never truthiness.","front_html":"Two coding rules for checks"}],"snippets":[["<span class=\"n\">Severity</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">Literal</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"CRITICAL\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"WARN\"</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>","","","<span class=\"nd\">@dataclass</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">frozen</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>","<span class=\"k\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">QaResult</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>","    <span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>","    <span class=\"n\">severity</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">Severity</span>","    <span class=\"n\">passed</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">bool</span>","    <span class=\"n\">observed</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">float</span> <span class=\"o\">|</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>"]],"takeaway_html":"Check at boundaries. Collect structured results. Log them all, then stop on CRITICAL.","title":"Validate at the boundaries, with severity"}],"pdf":"downloads/cheatsheets/cheatsheet-B5.pdf","summary":"Schema checks with pandera and input models with pydantic.","title":"Data validation"}
